<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mikhail Ermolaevich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mikhail Ermolaevich was a prince of Great Perm, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/komi-peoples">Komi</a> land on the upper Kama, in the 15th century. A baptised ruler who served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Grand Duchy of Moscow</a> while governing the local communities, he was taken prisoner when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> sent an army that captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cherdyn">Cherdyn</a> in 1472. Afterwards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> ruled Great Perm more directly, though his son Matvei was later allowed to rule as prince.</p></div>
